DECISION: APPROVED FOR PRODUCTION

Campaign: Cero 2.2.3 Linux Release
Priority: High
Objective: Build awareness of Cero's Linux release, communicate its practical value to developers, and drive GitHub visits and downloads.

Team delegation

@strategist — Define the positioning and messaging angle. Focus on Cero as an AI-powered terminal that asks before executing, now available in its Linux 2.2.3 release.

@researcher — Verify release details, identify Linux developer audience segments, and research relevant communities and distribution channels.

@blog-writer — Prepare a technical deep-dive explaining Cero's Linux release and its asks-first execution philosophy.

@writer — Draft the primary launch announcement, X thread (5 posts), and LinkedIn announcement.

@designer — Prepare launch-card concepts and specifications for 4:5, 1:1 and 16:9 formats using Magnm's brand identity.

@video-producer — Create a 30–45-second release reel using authentic Cero footage. No fabricated UI.

@reviewer — Verify every technical claim against Cero v2.2.3, check brand consistency and review all deliverables before approval.

@analyst — Define campaign KPIs: reach, engagement, GitHub traffic and release-page visits.

@growth — Recommend relevant Linux developer communities and launch experiments. No unsolicited spam.

Campaign messaging direction

Core message: Your terminal can understand natural language without blindly executing commands.

Creative angle: "Linux developers, meet Cero 2.2.3."

Primary CTA: Explore Cero on GitHub: https://github.com/NetPranav/Cero-Terminal

Execution rules

Use genuine Cero 2.2.3 Linux footage and verified release information.

Do not invent performance benchmarks or capabilities.

Do not introduce LazyLayout.

Submit all deliverables to the CMO for coordination.

Nothing gets published until the Reviewer clears it and the CEO gives final approval.

CMO decision: Proceed with the Linux release campaign. First deliver the messaging, research and creative concepts; then consolidate them into one campaign package for review.
